Package: bulkdeconv
Type: Package
Title: Cell-Type Deconvolution of Tumor Bulk RNA-Seq Through One Function
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Daiki", "Kumakura", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "55353329+DaikiKumakura@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Runs 24 published cell-type deconvolution and cell-abundance
    methods for bulk RNA-seq of tumor tissue (human or mouse) through a single
    function, bulkdeconv(data, expr, species, method). Nineteen methods are
    implemented in the package and run after installation, with their
    reference data included; those ported from existing code reproduce the
    output of the original implementations. The other five need one install
    step into a private library (their original packages, or for PUREE a
    downloaded model) and run each in its own R process. Input is
    checked before anything runs, a registry records what each method needs
    and how its output can be compared, and results come back in one standard
    layout with metadata and quality information. Only methods that need no
    registration are included.
